==Changelog - June 17th==
{{Collapsed section|18|CLICK HERE TO SHOW}}
'''Bank Tags'''

Bank Tags for mobile and the Official Client are here! 

* You can create up to 20 Bank Tags.
* To create a Bank Tag:
** Select the lil' + button in the top-left corner of your Bank
** Give your tag a title in the chat box that opens
** Next you'll get a search box where you can select an item to represent your tag as an icon
** Drag and drop an item from your main bank to your tag icon on the left to fill your tag
* To swap into your tag-view, simply select the icon and it'll pull up your tag. Tap or click it again to switch back to the bank.
* You can move your items around into any order you like, including leaving gaps or whole lines between items if you like.
* You can also duplicate tags by selecting duplicate from the minimenu, or if you're using a keyboard and mouse, you can hold shift while you drag an item and it'll spawn a new one.
** Unfortunately for you rare item collectors this only duplicates the tag not the item! You've still got to grind for those T-bows!
* Read more details in its dedicated section further down the blog.

====Leagues VI Rewards Tweaks====

* Made the head of Soulreaper Axe (o) larger, more befitting for its mighty makeover.
* The Demonic Pacts Throne Scroll no longer has a Construction level requirement to apply to a Demonic Throne.
* Equipping the two-handed League VI trophies and the Storm cruiser's coat will no longer form a tail behind you.
* The uncharged Toxic Trident (e) (o) has been made darker to make it more visually distinct from the Trident of the Swamp (e) (o). Also, the icons for the Trident of the Seas (o) has been rotated to match its non-ornamented version.
* Ornamenting the Trident of the Swamp, Trident of the Seas and Iban Staff now works in both ways: either by using the staves on their respective ornament kits, or by using the kits on the staves.
* The examine texts of Leagues VI trophies have been updated to reflect the extended end date of the Leagues.
* Not Demonic Pacts related, but still Leagues-related: Falo the Bard will now accept the Trailblazer Reloaded variant of the Infernal Axe (or) for his clue step asking for an Infernal Axe.

====Sailing Improvements====

* Added two new Slayer unlocks to Frost Dragons:
** '''Chance of Heavy Frost''': This unlock allows you to increase the ''weighting'' of Frost Dragon tasks from 5 to '''8''' on both Nieve and Duradel, making it more likely to receive these as tasks.
** '''I See Dragon''': This second unlock allows you to increase the ''task length'' of Frost Dragon Tasks, so you can keep slaying them for longer. Once this is unlocked, you'll be assigned between '''180 to 240''' Frost Dragons on both Nieve and Duradel.
** These unlocks cost '''100 Slayer Points''' each. Also, both of these unlocks can be disabled without a refund, should you prefer to.
* Bounty Task & Other Sailing Changes:
** Adjusted Bounty Tasks to ensure that their rewards better reflect participation.
** Players with multiple Bounty Tasks will also no longer receive multiple bounty item rolls from a single kill.
** Fixed a bug causing Veiled Kraken to give off-task rates while on a Bounty Task for the Dragon Cannon Barrel.
** Adjusted market values of several Sailing uniques to better align them with their current Grand Exchange prices.
** If you loot sea creatures while operating a cannon, you will no longer have to re-engage with the cannon. This means you'll now continue firing the cannon automatically after looting nearby sea creatures.
** If you are already overhealed from a Haddock and have between 100 and 108 Hitpoints, eating another Haddock will now correctly restore your Hitpoints to 109.

====Trouver System Rework====

* To reduce the chances of players losing crucial untradeables in the Wilderness, we've applied the following changes:
** Untradeables with ''no'' Combat benefits should never be lost on death,
** Untradeables with ''some'' Combat bonuses should break and need repairing without a Trouver parchment,
** Untradeables with ''strong'' Combat bonuses should need to be 'Trouvered' once, then never again.
* Untradeable items that previously didn't 'break', for example the Graceful set, will '''no longer be lost''' on death above Level 20 Wilderness.
* Untradeable items that previously broke will continue to break whether below or above level 20 Wilderness, but will no longer be lost. You'll continue to receive their 'broken' version and can repair them at Perdu for a small fee. Visit its dedicated section to see the items in this category.
* 'Higher tier' untradeables will continue to use the Trouver Parchment system, but with a crucial change: '''once a Trouver parchment has been used on an item, it will remain in that state forever''', the parchment will not be lost on death.
** On death '''below Level 20 Wilderness''' (or in PvP Worlds for fights at the Grand Exchange, for example), these higher tier items will simply break and be repairable with the current fee.
** On death '''above Level 20 Wilderness''', the item will become 'mangled' and require a higher fee of 500,000 GP to fix.
** You can still use the item on Perdu to remove the Trouver Parchment, should you wish to. Note that if you do not add a Trouver parchment to your 'higher tier' items, they will continue to be lost above 20 Wilderness.
* In cases where items are kitted using things like Ornament kits, the usual behaviour will occur and whoever kills you should receive the Ornament kit used, provided the Ornament kit is tradeable. For example, on death above Level 20 Wilderness, Dragon Defender (t) will break but it won't be lost, and the Dragon Defender Ornament Kit will go to the PKer.
* Though it didn't make it into this game update, there is one additional change we're working on: attempting to enter the Wilderness with any untradeable item that requires a Trouver Parchment to be protected will display a warning to make sure you're aware that you're risking an untradeable.

====Last Man Standing Changes====

* Added Dragon Crossbow and Opal Dragon Bolts (e) to the Max/Med loadout, and removed Rune Crossbow and Diamond Bolts (e).
* If you have the "Automatically smash empty vials" setting disabled, you will now keep the vials in your Inventory once a potion is fully consumed in Last Man Standing.
* Adjusted the default preset for players who have never played Last Man Standing before to have 3 Saradomin brews, 2 Sanfew serums and 10 sharks.
* Replaced the Berserker ring with the Berserker ring (i) in the starter kit for all builds.
* Set the default spellbook to Ancient Magicks if the player is brand new to the Last Man Standing gear setup.
* Zuriel's staff in Last Man Standing is now able to autocast Ancient Magicks spells as well.
* Added the Oathplate helm into the "Max/Med defensive" loot pool.
* Replaced the Dragon dagger with Dragon claws in the "Max/Med" starter kit.
* If sharks are dropped on the floor because the Inventory was entirely full, the sharks received when refilling your Inventory after a kill will stay on the floor only for 1 minute, as opposed to 10.

Additionally, we've also got a change for Emir's Arena:

* Added Ancient warriors' weapons to the list of items that can be used at Emir's Arena.

====Other Changes====

* Herb patches in Weiss and Trollheim now display what herb they contain.
* The hitbox on Huasca herbs now matches that of other herbs.
* Adjusted the Portal Nexus interface to make teleport options easier to read.
* The Blue Moon spear's special attack tooltip now refers to the Blue Moon set by its correct name.
* Fixed a bug where if a player used the special attack of Vesta's Spear (bh) and then switched weapons, ranged damage wasn't being blocked. Now, both melee and ranged damage are blocked regardless of whether or not the player has Vesta's Spear (bh) equipped after using its special attack. We have also changed Vesta's Spear (Deadman Mode) to have the same functionality.
* Level-up messages will no longer list the same spell multiple times when it is available through more than one spell book.
* The Bottomless Milk Bucket now works with the Zanaris Dairy Cow.
* On C++ client, if you have an active clue and the Clue Helper setting is on, the music player will now automatically scroll to the track you need to play for Cecilia.

Additionally, we've fixed various Z-buffer related graphical issues:

* The shadows of Penance Queen and its pet no longer flicker.
* Various NPC models across Gielinor (such as Prince Ali, Philippa, Watson, Freaky Forester etc) no longer have clipping issues.
* In Stronghold of Security, dropped items no longer clip into the ground.
* Bandos Godsword no longer clips with the table.
* Resolved flickering issues with the Hallowed Sepulchre pillars, Emir's Arena and Clan Wars portals, the entrances of Waterbirth Island Dungeon and Lovakengj Minecart Network.
* Guardians of the Rift statues and Prifddinas Agility Course Portal no longer flicker with the terrain.
* Dropped bones no longer clip with the carpets at Keep La Faye.
* Resolved flickering and clipping issues at the Kourend Castle Tower, Varrock bank roof, the snow-covered mountain within Stranglewood, Elemental Workshop Mind Chamber, Myths' Guild, the caves visited during the Recipe of Disaster quest and more.
* Fixed various clipping issues caused by intersecting levels and floors across Gielinor - for instance, Red Axe Caves.
* Fixed various clipping issues that occur when objects are on top of each other, such as pages on top of the crates in Red Axe Caves.
* The feet of player characters no longer clip into the floor at the Agility Pyramid, the Arceuus Library, the basement of the Varrock Museum,  grounds outside the southern entrance of Varrock, Lumbridge Castle kitchen and Shayzien Encampment wooden kits.
* The feet of birds in Tel Teklan no longer clip into surfaces.
* Fur rugs in the Ardougne Marketplace no longer phase into the ground.
* The QR code tiles in Shayzien are once again visible.

====PvP Rota====
The PvP rota has moved to '''Period A''':

