==Bank Tags==
===Bank Tags for mobile and the Official Client are here!===
[[File:Bank Tags, Trouver System Rework & More! (1).gif|thumb|450px|center|''If you can't see the gif above, click [https://cdn.runescape.com/assets/img/external/oldschool/2026/Newsposts/2026-05-29/BankTags2.gif here]!'']]

Pre-plan your gear, lay out your pots and food for easy access and be ready to take on whatever content you're heading to next.

Before using the Bank Tags, make sure you have the mobile app and the Official Client updated to the latest version. And if you have used Bank Tags before updating, you will need to delete all Bank Tags using the functionality provided.

===Creating Bank Tags===
[[File:Bank Tags, Trouver System Rework & More! (2).mp4|thumb|600px|center|''If you can't see the video above, click [https://cdn.runescape.com/assets/img/external/oldschool/2026/Newsposts/2026-06-17/banktags.mp4 here]!'']]

Creating a Bank Tag is super simple. You'll now find a little + button in the top-left corner of your Bank. Selecting this will open up a chat box where you can give your tag a title. Our usual chat filters apply here, and you can use up to 25 alphanumeric characters. 

Following your feedback from the Summer Campfire, we've increased the total tags you can create to 20. Hopefully this feels like more breathing room to cover all your bases.

Next you'll get a search box where you can select an item to represent your tag as an icon. You can use pretty much any item in the game, both tradeable and untradeable. 

Then, it's time to fill your tag! It's as easy as dragging and dropping an item from your main bank to your tag icon on the left. It'll drop in there ready for you to organise your layout. 

To swap into your tag-view, simply select the icon and it'll pull up your tag. Tap or click it again to switch back to the bank. You can move your items around into any order you like, including leaving gaps or whole lines between items if you like. You can also duplicate tags by selecting duplicate from the minimenu, or if you're using a keyboard and mouse, you can hold shift while you drag an item and it'll spawn a new one! 

Unfortunately for you rare item collectors this only duplicates the tag not the item, you've still got to grind for those T-bows!
[[File:Bank Tags, Trouver System Rework & More! (3).jpg|thumb|400px|center|''If you can't see the image above, click [https://cdn.runescape.com/assets/img/external/oldschool/2026/Newsposts/2026-06-17/manifesting.jpg here]!'']]

Removing an item from a tag is as easy as selecting "remove from tag" from the minimenu. You can delete the whole tag by opening the tag's minimenu and selecting "delete tag". You'll get a warning message first so there's no accidental misclicks! 

You can also drag your tags up and down the list so your favourite or current activity tags are right at your fingertips. 

It's pretty much as easy as that! You will see a few more or a few less tags depending on whether you have the incinerator active, Potion Storage and/or Group Ironman Storage. We've popped a couple of screenshots below so you know what to expect.
[[File:Bank Tags, Trouver System Rework & More! (4).png|thumb|250px|center|''If you can't see the image above, click [https://cdn.runescape.com/assets/img/external/oldschool/2026/Newsposts/2026-06-17/tags1.png here]!'']]

