===FAQs===
We caught a few questions being asked after our announcement, and we know it can be tricky to track those answers down spread across various platforms and comment replies. So, here are our answers all rounded up into one spot, and we'll keep this updated as we see more coming through.

====How do Bank Tags interact with Potion Storage?====
Right now, they act as two different entities. So if you want to make a tag with any potions, or to withdraw then via your tag, you'll need to make sure they're in your bank-proper, as opposed to the storage.

====Will these tags affect any Bank Tags I have in approved third-party clients?====
Nope! This system is only being implemented on our C++ client and mobile, meaning any approved third-party client tags will be completely unaffected. 

====Will tags interfere with my main bank at all?====
No, whatever happens in a tag, stays in a tag! So you won't see any movement or separation in your main bank. Obviously any withdrawals will affect both, as the tag is merely a representation of your item.

===Known Issues===

* There is a known issue of duplicate icons appearing when searching for a suitable Bank Tag icon, we will resolve this in a future update.

If you do come across any issues not listed here, please drop us a message on Reddit or Discord in the Official Client section!

===Wrapping up===
We're so excited to get Bank Tags in your hands! We'll be keeping up with feedback so make sure you share your thoughts.

