==Sailing Improvements==
===New Slayer Unlocks for Frost Dragons===
The proposed Slayer unlocks from our <u>[https://secure.runescape.com/m=news/sailing-update-buffs-changes--more?oldschool=1 Sailing buffs blog]</u> are now here!

We've added two new Slayer unlocks to Frost Dragons:

* '''Chance of Heavy Frost''': This unlock allows you to increase the ''weighting ''of Frost Dragon tasks from 5 to '''8''' on both Nieve and Duradel, making it more likely to receive these as tasks.
* '''I See Dragon''': This second unlock allows you to increase the ''task length'' of Frost Dragon Tasks, so you can keep slaying them for longer. Once this is unlocked, you'll be assigned between '''180 to 240''' Frost Dragons on both Nieve and Duradel.
[[File:Bank Tags, Trouver System Rework & More! (11).png|thumb|250px|center|''If you can't see the image above, click [https://cdn.runescape.com/assets/img/external/oldschool/2026/Newsposts/2026-06-17/unlock.png here]!'']]

These unlocks cost '''100 Slayer Points''' each. Also, both of these unlocks can be disabled without a refund, should you prefer to.

===Bounty Task Changes===
We'll be making some adjustments to Bounty Tasks to ensure that their rewards better reflect participation.

First, the chance of receiving rewards and unique drops from bounty creatures will now scale based on your contribution towards killing the creature. Players who contribute more damage towards a kill will have a greater chance of receiving these rewards, while players who contribute less will have a proportionally lower chance.

This change applies to unique drops from:

* Great White Sharks
* Armoured Krakens
* Vampyre Krakens
* Veiled Krakens
* Orcas
* Narwhals

Players with multiple Bounty Tasks will also no longer receive multiple Bounty item rolls from a single kill. Players can only progress one Bounty Task at a time, but having multiple tasks will allow players to extend their trips for longer.

We've also fixed a bug causing Veiled Kraken to give off-task rates while on a Bounty Task for the Dragon Cannon Barrel.

===Other Sailing Changes===
Last but not least, we're adjusting the market values of several Sailing uniques to better align them with their current Grand Exchange prices. This is to ensure they work with existing systems that rely on an item's market value, such as Death's Coffer.

The item value adjustment change will affect: 

* Large Dragon Keel Parts
* Dragon Keel Parts
* Dragon Metal Sheets
* Bottled Storms
* Inky Paint
* Broken Dragon Hooks
* Dragon Cannon Barrel

Please note, these changes won't affect their Grand Exchange prices.

Additional Sailing improvements:

* If you loot sea creatures while operating a cannon, you will no longer have to re-engage with the cannon. This means you'll now continue firing the cannon automatically after looting nearby sea creatures.
* If you are already overhealed from a Haddock and have between 100 and 108 Hitpoints, eating another Haddock will now correctly restore your Hitpoints to 109.

==Trouver System Rework==
We're bringing you the proposed changes to the Trouver System from <u>[https://secure.runescape.com/m=news/gathering-qol-trouver-changes--more?oldschool=1 this blog]</u> back in April. For those who don't know what 'Trouver' means, you can check out the blog for a detailed explanation. In a nutshell, a Trouver parchment allows you to "lock" your untradeable items by using them on Perdu, preventing them from being lost on PvP death. However, once you've died, the Trouver parchment would be lost. It's easy to forget to re-lock your untradeables after dying, which can result in permanently losing them the next time you're PKed.

To reduce the chances of players losing crucial untradeables in the Wilderness, we've applied the following changes. The general rule of thumb here is:


* Untradeables with ''no'' Combat benefits should never be lost on death,
* Untradeables with ''some'' Combat bonuses should break and need repairing without a Trouver parchment,
* Untradeables with ''strong'' Combat bonuses should need to be 'Trouvered' once, then never again.

First, untradeable items that previously didn't 'break', for example the Graceful set, will '''no longer be lost''' on death above Level 20 Wilderness. [https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/(l)?_gl=1*bpeirl*_gcl_au*MTkzNDY2MTU0LjE3Nzg0ODc4MjU. This applies to any untradeable item that isn't found on this list.]

Second, untradeable items that previously broke will continue to break whether below or above level 20 Wilderness, but will no longer be lost. You'll continue to receive their 'broken' version and can repair them at Perdu for a small fee. The items in this category are:
